cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the CellTune
  paper (doi:10.1038/s41592-026-03162-2), whose human-in-the-loop workflow this
  extension derives functions from. Depending on which features you use, please
  also cite the relevant method papers listed under "references".
title: "SP Classify: an active-learning cell classifier extension for QuPath"
abstract: >-
  A QuPath extension for classifying cells in highly multiplexed images. It trains two
  different gradient-boosted models on manually labelled cells, then uses their disagreement
  to pick the most informative cells for review, so a usable classifier can be built from a
  few hundred labels rather than thousands.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mckay
    given-names: Michael
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-2447-9506"
    affiliation: "Walter and Eliza Hall Institute of Medical Research"
# Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest release. Use this rather than a
# version-specific DOI so citations do not go stale.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21782421
version: 0.3.1
date-released: "2026-09-05"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/mikemcka/qupath-extension-sp-classify"
keywords:
  - QuPath
  - multiplexed imaging
  - cell classification
  - active learning
  - spatial biology
  - image analysis
  - machine learning
  - bioimage analysis
# Method papers whose algorithms this extension reimplements. Cite the ones whose
# corresponding feature you actually use in your analysis.
